OL,3,CExcitement builds as skygazers prepare
OL,4,Cto witness best solar eclipse since
OL,5,C1999
OL,7,FExcitement is building all over the
OL,8,Fworld as millions of people prepare to
OL,9,Fcast their eyes to the sky to try and
OL,10,Fwitness the best solar eclipse in
OL,11,Falmost thirty years.
OL,13,FMore than 90% of the sun will be
OL,14,Fobscured by the moon on Wednesday
OL,15,Fevening between 6.17pm and 8.06pm, the
OL,16,Fmost it has been blocked in the UK
OL,17,Fsince the 1999 total eclipse.
OL,19,FIt is due to begin in Siberia, Russia,
OL,20,Fbefore becoming visible in Alaska,
OL,21,FGreenland and Europe.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
